Links in `PostIndex.md` are hardcoded to `https://xentaxbackup.github.io/markdown/...`. When the backup site is served from `https://asasasasasbc.github.io/BUXeNTaXBackup.github.io/`, clicking any post link navigates away to the original domain instead of staying within the current deployment.

## Changes

- **Link rewriting post-render**: After markdown is rendered, all `<a href>` attributes pointing to `xentaxbackup.github.io` are rewritten to absolute paths prefixed with `BASE`:
  ```js
  // https://xentaxbackup.github.io/markdown/Sorry_26922
  // → /BUXeNTaXBackup.github.io/markdown/Sorry_26922
  var xentaxRe = new RegExp('^https?://' + XENTAX_ORIGIN + '(\\/.*)?$', 'i');
  document.querySelectorAll('#content a[href]').forEach(function(a) {
    var match = a.getAttribute('href').match(xentaxRe);
    if (match) a.setAttribute('href', BASE + (match[1] || '/'));
  });
  ```

- **SPA click handler on `#content`**: Intercepts clicks on rewritten links (absolute paths starting with `/`), calls `pushState`, and invokes `loadPage()` — no full-page reload. The existing `<base href="./">` ensures `fetch()` always resolves `.md` files relative to `index.html`'s origin regardless of the displayed URL.

- **`XENTAX_ORIGIN` constant**: Extracted the target domain as a named constant at the top of the script for easier maintenance.

