Android app still crashes after PR #103's Samsung fix. Three distinct crash vectors remain.

### Cross-thread framework state access in `updateOrientation()`

`ScreenStack.CurrentScreen` and `PlayingState.Value` were read inside a `RunOnUiThread` lambda — wrong thread for osu-framework state. Moved reads to the update thread; only the `RequestedOrientation` assignment is dispatched:

```csharp
// Before: framework state read on Android UI thread (race condition)
gameActivity.RunOnUiThread(() =>
{
    if (ScreenStack.CurrentScreen is not IOsuScreen currentScreen) return;
    var orientation = MobileUtils.GetOrientation(this, currentScreen, ...);
    gameActivity.RequestedOrientation = ...;
});

// After: framework state read on update thread, only UI mutation dispatched
if (ScreenStack?.CurrentScreen is not IOsuScreen currentScreen) return;
var orientation = MobileUtils.GetOrientation(this, currentScreen, ...);
gameActivity.RunOnUiThread(() => { gameActivity.RequestedOrientation = ...; });
```

### Two-level deferred type loading in `AndroidNativeBridgeManager`

PR #103 boxed `AndroidNativeBridgeManager` as `object?` in `OsuGameAndroid` to prevent eager type resolution. But `AndroidNativeBridgeManager` itself still declared `OboeAudioBridge?` / `VulkanProbe?` fields — loading the manager class triggers `NativeLibrary.TryLoad` via their static constructors. This crashes on Samsung when a native setting was persisted as `true` from a previous session (config replay during `LoadComplete`).

Applied the same `object?` + `[MethodImpl(NoInlining)]` pattern inside the bridge manager so `OboeAudioBridge` and `VulkanProbe` are only resolved when their specific feature method is invoked.

### Fragile `Dispose`

- `OsuGameAndroid.Dispose`: `base.Dispose` throwing would skip native bridge cleanup. Wrapped in `try/finally`.
- `AndroidNativeBridgeManager.Dispose`: per-bridge `try/catch` so one failure doesn't leak the other.

